WEBVTT

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:16.860
Atsushi... you know...

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:19.240
There's something I've been 
thinking about lately.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:20.660
What is it, En-chan?

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:21.620
The Ol*mpics?

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:22.440
The constitution?

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:23.290
Chikuwabu?

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:25.250
No, time.

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:26.750
Time?

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:29.500
We only just got promoted to 3rd years,

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:31.400
and it was autumn before we knew it.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:34.380
We missed all our chances for summer fun.

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:35.600
You know?

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:37.850
Not true, Yufuin-senpai.

00:00:38.710 --> 00:00:39.660
We went to both

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:42.720
Danran Beach and Mt. Binan.

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:46.270
Is your memory getting fuzzy already? 
That's an aging danger sign!

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:49.400
En-chan, your kouhai are worried about you.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:50.410
Yeah,

00:00:50.410 --> 00:00:53.240
but it didn't feel like we were going 
to the mountains or the beach for fun.

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:55.840
It's too late now,

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:59.200
but it's always been my dream to 
make lots of fun summer memories.

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:01.540
You know the saying.

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:04.080
"Time doesn't betray dreams," and vice versa.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:05.790
Does anyone even know what that means?

00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:09.570
In my opinion, it means that 
the time you spend working

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:12.470
puts you that much closer to your dreams...

00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:14.510
Atsushi. You don't actually 
have to analyze it.

00:01:14.770 --> 00:01:16.470
Hey, you know sand clocks?

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:18.800
That's pretty out of the blue.

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:21.410
Well, talking about clocks 
in the bath reminded me.

00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:22.500
Sand clocks.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:24.800
Saunas have them a lot, don't they?

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:27.260
Io, have you been to a sauna?

00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:29.250
A friend of mine has one at home.

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:30.850
A Finnish sauna.

00:01:30.850 --> 00:01:32.380
It's basically a steam bath.

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:36.090
They slap their backs with 
birch branches, don't they?

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:37.710
What? Do they?

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:38.930
You didn't know?

00:01:38.930 --> 00:01:41.520
Anyway, Ryuu, what were 
you saying about sand clocks?

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:42.710
With a sand clock, you know?

00:01:42.710 --> 00:01:45.250
It's a clock, but it doesn't 
tell you what time it is.

00:01:46.150 --> 00:01:47.910
It claims to be a time-telling device,

00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:50.360
but it won't actually tell you the time.

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:51.960
So how is it a clock?

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:55.170
But isn't that true of a stopwatch, as well?

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:56.550
Oh, right.

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:58.970
But somehow that just doesn't sit right.

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:01.880
A sand clock is known as 
an "hourglass" in English.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:03.570
It's not a watch or a clock.

00:02:03.570 --> 00:02:05.990
Sand and glass? They're the same thing!

00:02:05.990 --> 00:02:07.180
I can't believe you guys

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:10.190
kept this stupid conversation up this long.

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:13.080
En-chan, are you really one to talk?

00:02:13.630 --> 00:02:14.400
What do you mean?

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:20.160
You use a sand clock when 
you get an enema, right?

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:21.320
Enema?!

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:22.610
Because after it goes in,

00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:25.290
you need to hold it in for a while.

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:26.590
Really?

00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:29.500
I never knew sand clocks 
bore such a noble mission.

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:30.940
But Yumoto,

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:33.280
why do you know something so hardcore?

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:35.430
Well, when I was little, my big brother would always make me...

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:37.090
We don't need to hear this.

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:39.010
They never change.

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:41.120
That Earth Defense Club!

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:44.140
You know, you're a member of it, too...

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:48.700
I knew it!

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:50.080
You're all here, eh?

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:51.380
Hey there.

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:52.860
Come on in!

00:02:53.270 --> 00:02:55.230
What do you mean, you knew it?

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:59.180
The Earth Defense Club

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:01.950
can always be found marinating 
at Kurotama Bath.

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:03.660
Excellent observation.

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:11.090
I initially turned up my nose at 
the thought of public bathing.

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:13.420
But it's quite nice when you get used to it.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:15.290
Right?

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:18.050
You can't stretch out in the bath at home.

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:18.940
Go on!

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:21.520
Sink right in down to your shoulders!

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:23.840
Our hot water comes right from a hot spring!

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:25.300
Hey.

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:34.320
It's been a while.

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:36.650
We see each other in school every day.

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:37.410
Oh.

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:38.630
That's right.

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:42.110
I guess it's been hard, huh?

00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:43.540
What has?

00:03:44.210 --> 00:03:46.410
Well... you know...

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:47.730
stuff?

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:49.230
"Stuff"?

00:03:49.590 --> 00:03:50.680
That's incredibly vague.

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:52.400
True...

00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:55.720
That reminds me.

00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:58.720
Aren't you student council 
guys gonna study abroad?

00:03:58.720 --> 00:03:59.720
Hey!

00:03:58.720 --> 00:03:59.720
Hush!

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:01.190
Yeah.

00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:02.370
We head out tomorrow.

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:03.630
Lucky!

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:07.400
You know, I've never ever been on a plane!

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:09.400
What does it feel like?

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:12.270
You just fly, like normal.

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:13.640
Come on!

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:16.650
But what's normal? That's I want to know!

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:18.080
Is it exciting?

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:19.480
Is it invigorating?!

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:21.040
It's not...

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:22.680
especially exciting.

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:24.880
Nor is it invigorating, I suppose.

00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:26.450
I don't really know.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:29.480
Yumoto! Yumoto!

00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:30.280
What?

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:32.140
Just get over here!

00:04:32.140 --> 00:04:33.400
Okay...

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:36.750
Leave the two of them alone.

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:37.430
What?

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:39.460
Here, you mean?

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:40.950
Yes, here!

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:41.710
Why?

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:43.370
Because!

00:04:43.370 --> 00:04:45.910
Arima-san, have you finished 
your preparations?

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:47.180
More or less.

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:49.660
It doesn't feel real to me yet.

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:52.750
Same here.

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:55.450
But it's even worse for Kinshiro, I believe.

00:04:57.720 --> 00:04:59.650
You seem rather busy.

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:02.110
No, things are pretty normal here.

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:13.950
Tomorrow—

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:13.950
How about—

00:05:14.170 --> 00:05:15.310
What?

00:05:15.310 --> 00:05:16.360
Nothing.

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:18.420
Tomorrow what?

00:05:18.670 --> 00:05:19.720
Tomorrow...

00:05:20.280 --> 00:05:22.380
I was wondering if anything was going on.

00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:24.280
With me?

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:26.590
Well, you're flying out, right, Kin-chan?

00:05:26.790 --> 00:05:28.560
No, not that.

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:29.850
I mean overall.

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:31.430
Overall?

00:05:31.710 --> 00:05:33.110
I don't know.

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:36.640
Look at this!

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:39.040
It's hell! Sweet and sour pastry hell!

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:40.170
Just say it!

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:41.370
Say "I'll go see you off!"

00:05:41.370 --> 00:05:42.460
Say "Come and see me off!"

00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:44.280
Hey, back off.

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:47.060
The ice just started melting after so long.

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:49.210
Our job is just to watch and hope for the best.

00:05:49.210 --> 00:05:51.090
Something that's been balled up
 for so many years

00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:53.180
won't untangle that easily.

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:54.930
You said it, Arima-san.

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:56.960
Huh? What do you mean?

00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:58.280
What won't untangle?

00:05:58.280 --> 00:06:00.830
Never mind! You just sit!

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:04.420
But President Kusatsu

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:06.550
looks a lot like Mr. Tawarayama right now!

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:09.910
You mean the blank expression? 
That's typical for him.

00:06:09.910 --> 00:06:11.010
Yeah...

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:12.140
No!

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:14.960
I mean he's floating, with Atsushi-senpai!

00:06:17.630 --> 00:06:19.000
Did they pass out from the heat?

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:20.210
President!

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:27.780
Love, Once More!

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:32.020
Knowing Atsushi,

00:06:32.020 --> 00:06:34.540
he felt awkward pushing to come see him off

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:36.290
when he wasn't invited.

00:06:36.290 --> 00:06:37.610
And Kinshiro probably thought

00:06:37.610 --> 00:06:39.130
asking him to come see him off

00:06:39.130 --> 00:06:42.210
would be a shameless request.

00:06:42.410 --> 00:06:44.040
They could have just said it.

00:06:44.930 --> 00:06:46.670
Why didn't they say it?

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:49.470
Things are complicated 
when you're a grown-up.

00:06:51.910 --> 00:06:53.660
Are you awake, Kinshiro?

00:06:55.820 --> 00:06:57.270
Are you okay?

00:06:57.840 --> 00:06:59.440
I seem to have fainted.

00:06:59.930 --> 00:07:01.810
I'm sorry for the trouble.

00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:07.900
Atsushi-senpai's not awake yet!

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:08.960
Well,

00:07:09.500 --> 00:07:11.020
I have to get home soon

00:07:11.020 --> 00:07:12.400
to get ready for tomorrow.

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:13.500
Here!

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:14.370
Thank you.

00:07:15.020 --> 00:07:17.390
Now, Earth Defense Club.

00:07:17.390 --> 00:07:20.580
Please try not to cause any 
trouble while we're abroad.

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:21.680
Oh, yeah!

00:07:21.680 --> 00:07:24.540
Could we come to see you off tomorrow?

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:27.910
I want to see a plane!

00:07:27.910 --> 00:07:28.920
Can we?

00:07:30.480 --> 00:07:32.350
What should we do, President?

00:07:32.350 --> 00:07:34.340
If you want to come, do so.

00:07:34.340 --> 00:07:36.900
We have no authority to stop you.

00:07:36.900 --> 00:07:38.930
Well, I guess that's that.

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:39.890
See you.

00:07:40.590 --> 00:07:41.650
Yes!

00:07:42.390 --> 00:07:44.450
Atsushi, you okay?

00:07:44.450 --> 00:07:46.570
The student council just left.

00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:48.480
I know.

00:07:49.060 --> 00:07:49.900
Yumoto...

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:52.320
Thanks.

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:53.570
For what?

00:07:53.570 --> 00:07:55.360
Well... nothing.

00:07:56.230 --> 00:07:58.900
Atsushi-senpai, are you cold?

00:07:58.900 --> 00:08:00.900
Should we go back in?

00:08:00.900 --> 00:08:01.950
Sure.

00:08:01.950 --> 00:08:03.910
I don't have any dates to go on today.

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:06.340
And the Tokyo markets are already closed.

00:08:11.480 --> 00:08:13.440
Atsushi, you're way too dere.

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:14.880
Me?

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:15.760
Really?

00:08:17.870 --> 00:08:19.460
I was thinking, in hindsight,

00:08:19.990 --> 00:08:23.380
the Battle Lovers wasn't bad at all.

00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:24.410
You think?

00:08:24.410 --> 00:08:26.690
These things are the root of all evil.

00:08:26.930 --> 00:08:29.040
I know, that's why I said "in hindsight."

00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:31.650
All's well that ends well, you know?

00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:34.650
Kinugawa-senpai, you're really generous.

00:08:34.650 --> 00:08:36.670
Very far-sighted thinking.

00:08:36.670 --> 00:08:39.390
I had fun with our Battle 
Lover club activity, too!

00:08:39.390 --> 00:08:40.620
Don't call it a club activity!

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:44.370
We just need Wom-san 
and Mr. Tawarayama to show up,

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:45.940
and we'll have the whole gang!

00:08:46.890 --> 00:08:48.330
Speak of the devil.

00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:50.000
Wom-san?

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:52.670
I am...

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:52.670
An hourglass!

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:54.770
Don't call me by such a cheap name!

00:08:54.770 --> 00:08:56.160
I am...

00:08:55.390 --> 00:08:56.740
Hourglass Monster!

00:08:56.740 --> 00:08:57.930
Silence!

00:08:57.930 --> 00:09:00.060
I mean, stop time!

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:02.980
I am wonderful!

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:07.470
Evolution, change, 
and growth are unnecessary!

00:09:07.470 --> 00:09:10.120
I live now only for this moment!

00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:11.300
Live! For! The present!

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:12.780
Life Now!

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:16.110
Did you behold my power?

00:09:16.940 --> 00:09:18.620
Time Stopper!

00:09:19.380 --> 00:09:21.140
Wow, he startled me!

00:09:21.140 --> 00:09:23.500
He startled me so much I forgot to breathe!

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:25.950
He's sounding kind of cool, though...

00:09:25.950 --> 00:09:28.000
You think that's cool? Really?

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.000
I mean, I know "Show Stopper"...

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:32.150
But why a monster?

00:09:32.150 --> 00:09:34.820
I thought we beat Zundar and Hireashi.

00:09:34.820 --> 00:09:37.010
He should have been demoted to assistant director.

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:39.180
You intend to stand against us, do you?

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:40.530
Senpais!

00:09:40.530 --> 00:09:43.180
Let's Love Making into the Battle Lovers!

00:09:43.590 --> 00:09:45.230
Love Making!

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:46.890
I don't think so!

00:09:54.020 --> 00:09:56.360
The Lovracelets... disappeared?

00:09:57.200 --> 00:10:01.830
<b>Messenger of Love From Space
Wombat
Special Abilities:
 Highly Advanced Scientific Technology</b>

00:10:08.490 --> 00:10:10.790
Wow, you can really see the tan line!

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:12.290
Focus on the real issue!

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:15.340
Attention, Battle Lovers!

00:10:15.640 --> 00:10:17.550
Your time ends now.

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:18.860
For, you see...

00:10:18.860 --> 00:10:21.420
I will end you all!

00:10:21.870 --> 00:10:22.920
Wait!

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:27.260
How did you know we're the Battle Lovers?

00:10:29.750 --> 00:10:31.550
That's not all I know!

00:10:31.550 --> 00:10:34.110
Your faces and voices are blur-free

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:35.780
and exposed!

00:10:36.470 --> 00:10:37.240
No way!

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:39.220
Yes way!

00:10:41.630 --> 00:10:42.620
En-chan!

00:10:42.840 --> 00:10:45.100
I don't know who you're working for,

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:48.120
but this is a violation of privacy laws!

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:51.790
You won't need privacy when you're dead!

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:53.020
Why, you...

00:10:53.020 --> 00:10:54.530
We won't let you...

00:10:55.160 --> 00:10:56.250
I can't move!

00:10:56.450 --> 00:10:57.530
En-chan!

00:10:57.810 --> 00:10:58.820
Darn it.

00:10:58.820 --> 00:11:00.420
This weirdo wouldn't be able

00:11:00.420 --> 00:11:03.140
to push us around if we could Love Making!

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:05.640
Sorry, but that's not in your futures!

00:11:05.880 --> 00:11:08.350
Sleep in the hour of repose known as death!

00:11:14.650 --> 00:11:17.610
Is someone horsing around in the bath?!

00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:19.530
Who are you?!

00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:20.960
Big bro!

00:11:21.550 --> 00:11:23.320
And he's kicking sand around, too!

00:11:23.720 --> 00:11:26.490
What the hell made you think that was okay?!

00:11:26.760 --> 00:11:28.930
Well...

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:32.210
Oh, there's a very important galaxy-spanning reason...

00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:34.020
Someone who can't wash off

00:11:34.020 --> 00:11:36.500
before getting in the bath, 
talking about the galaxy?!

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:38.630
What kind of crap is that?!

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:40.030
I'm sorry!

00:11:40.030 --> 00:11:42.010
I'll come back later!

00:11:42.420 --> 00:11:43.300
Hold on!

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:44.720
Clean this up first!

00:11:45.560 --> 00:11:46.560
Yumoto.

00:11:46.820 --> 00:11:47.510
Yes?

00:11:47.860 --> 00:11:49.380
Choose better friends.

00:11:50.860 --> 00:11:51.810
What?

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:53.350
Don't tell the student council?

00:11:53.570 --> 00:11:54.910
Why not?

00:11:54.910 --> 00:11:57.170
They're about to go study abroad.

00:11:57.170 --> 00:11:59.070
I don't want to worry them.

00:11:59.460 --> 00:12:03.450
But what if Zundar's 
pulling the strings again?

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:04.740
No way.

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:07.030
Kin-chan wouldn't do anything so cowardly.

00:12:07.770 --> 00:12:08.990
Sorry.

00:12:10.680 --> 00:12:12.580
You have nothing to apologize for, Ryuu.

00:12:12.940 --> 00:12:15.500
But if they're not behind it,

00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:17.920
we have to figure out what 
the hell happened yesterday.

00:12:19.430 --> 00:12:21.010
En-chan, what's wrong?

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:23.720
<b>{white}Monthly 
{red}Shounen GUNP</b>

00:12:23.920 --> 00:12:26.390
Hey! That's my GUNP!

00:12:27.110 --> 00:12:28.990
You snuck up on me! You cowards!

00:12:28.990 --> 00:12:31.560
No, you just weren't paying attention.

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:32.350
Give it back!

00:12:37.930 --> 00:12:38.690
Ryuu!

00:12:39.040 --> 00:12:40.720
Time Stopping Monster-san!

00:12:40.720 --> 00:12:42.400
We'd like a word with you.

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:44.360
Oh? I'll hear you out.

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:46.580
What, he's okay being called <i>that</i>?

00:12:46.580 --> 00:12:50.250
We need to go and see off 
some friends at the airport.

00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:51.610
You can read that if you want,

00:12:51.610 --> 00:12:53.580
so can we meet you back here?

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:55.850
Huh? That's my GUNP!

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:55.850
I see!

00:12:55.850 --> 00:12:57.960
Stop the time on the fight, then?

00:12:58.200 --> 00:12:58.910
That's right!

00:12:58.910 --> 00:12:59.960
Exactly!

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:01.250
It won't be that easy!

00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:04.150
Hey! My GUNP!

00:13:04.150 --> 00:13:05.130
That's property damage!

00:13:05.130 --> 00:13:06.090
Now you'll pay!

00:13:06.090 --> 00:13:08.650
Although we always intended to make you pay!

00:13:10.280 --> 00:13:13.950
Hey, quit getting sand 
all over the club room!

00:13:14.300 --> 00:13:15.100
Wait!

00:13:15.300 --> 00:13:17.600
Without your Love Power,

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:19.460
you are no match for me!

00:13:23.900 --> 00:13:24.780
Look at that.

00:13:25.260 --> 00:13:27.740
They're as pathetic as turtles 
turned over onto their backs.

00:13:27.940 --> 00:13:29.190
Stop it.

00:13:29.190 --> 00:13:30.610
That's an insult...

00:13:30.610 --> 00:13:31.700
to the turtles.

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:34.060
That's right. They're less than turtles.

00:13:34.060 --> 00:13:35.440
Yes,

00:13:35.440 --> 00:13:37.420
they're pathetic water fleas.

00:13:37.640 --> 00:13:40.380
They'll be pulverized, at this rate.

00:13:45.770 --> 00:13:49.450
Now... It's time to end this!

00:13:50.520 --> 00:13:53.850
Hey! Hold on a minute!

00:13:54.770 --> 00:13:55.850
That voice!

00:14:01.600 --> 00:14:05.610
I'm here!

00:14:04.480 --> 00:14:05.610
Wom-san!

00:14:05.840 --> 00:14:08.040
My name is Wombat.

00:14:08.040 --> 00:14:09.110
The messenger of love,

00:14:09.110 --> 00:14:11.530
who loves the Earth and protects it!

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:13.030
Wh-What?!

00:14:13.250 --> 00:14:14.030
What?

00:14:14.030 --> 00:14:17.100
You used to say you weren't a wombat.

00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:20.500
Now that I am here, there's no need to fear!

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:23.230
You who are without love...

00:14:23.230 --> 00:14:26.260
At last, love is... love will...

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:31.520
Wom-san, you're so wriggly!

00:14:31.520 --> 00:14:33.680
Anyway, put these on already!

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:41.150
I thought something like this might happen,

00:14:41.340 --> 00:14:44.110
so here are your new True Lovracelets!

00:14:44.350 --> 00:14:46.800
He thought something 
like this might happen?

00:14:47.070 --> 00:14:49.820
We have to transform again?

00:14:49.820 --> 00:14:51.460
<i>Of course!</i>

00:14:51.460 --> 00:14:53.030
Let's go, everyone!

00:14:54.030 --> 00:14:55.650
Love Making!

00:15:21.450 --> 00:15:22.940
The Sparkling Prince!

00:15:24.110 --> 00:15:26.230
Battle Lover Scarlet!

00:15:26.960 --> 00:15:28.570
Love Making.

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:39.040
The Flashing Prince!

00:15:39.460 --> 00:15:41.060
Battle Lover Cerulean!

00:15:42.190 --> 00:15:43.650
Love Making.

00:15:51.820 --> 00:15:53.220
The Piercing Prince!

00:15:53.730 --> 00:15:55.590
Battle Lover Epinard!

00:15:56.930 --> 00:15:58.240
Love Making.

00:16:06.760 --> 00:16:08.200
The Roaring Prince!

00:16:08.690 --> 00:16:10.280
Battle Lover Sulfur!

00:16:11.390 --> 00:16:12.940
Love Making!

00:16:21.830 --> 00:16:22.660
The Thrilling Prince!

00:16:23.320 --> 00:16:25.080
Battle Lover Vesta!

00:16:25.740 --> 00:16:27.530
This love-filled planet

00:16:27.530 --> 00:16:29.500
will not abide those who lack love!

00:16:29.700 --> 00:16:31.470
Those who wield loveless power

00:16:31.470 --> 00:16:33.220
must kneel before love!

00:16:33.460 --> 00:16:34.810
Love is power!

00:16:34.810 --> 00:16:36.430
Love is hope!

00:16:36.680 --> 00:16:38.100
Be born for love!

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:39.890
Give your life for love!

00:16:40.220 --> 00:16:40.940
Love!

00:16:40.940 --> 00:16:43.560
We are, forever, the heirs 
to the throne of love...

00:16:44.070 --> 00:16:45.310
Battle Lovers!

00:16:45.630 --> 00:16:47.180
Feel the power...

00:16:47.520 --> 00:16:48.990
of love!

00:16:50.440 --> 00:16:53.260
What? Did our costumes change?

00:16:53.260 --> 00:16:55.400
Yeah, they're different from before!

00:16:56.550 --> 00:16:59.240
In season 2, 
your items and designs always change.

00:16:59.240 --> 00:17:01.000
That is the law of the universe!

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:03.820
The providence of nature!

00:17:04.180 --> 00:17:06.250
And it's not just how they look!

00:17:06.460 --> 00:17:08.380
You've also powered up,

00:17:08.380 --> 00:17:11.590
and you boast a far more vivid design,

00:17:11.590 --> 00:17:15.050
invoking a taste of the 
"now" and the "young"!

00:17:16.480 --> 00:17:20.280
I've given up looking 
for taste from this guy.

00:17:20.280 --> 00:17:23.070
Let's just beat this thing 
and get to the airport.

00:17:23.070 --> 00:17:23.520
Yeah.

00:17:24.100 --> 00:17:25.770
Cerulean Love Aqua!

00:17:29.230 --> 00:17:29.900
Curse you!

00:17:30.050 --> 00:17:32.360
En-chan-senpai! I'll do it too!

00:17:32.980 --> 00:17:35.360
Scarlet Love Lumiere!

00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:39.120
Yeah! Go! Do it!

00:17:39.270 --> 00:17:41.370
Vesta Love Ignit!

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:43.490
I beg your pardon!

00:17:43.490 --> 00:17:45.040
Sulfur Love Gaia!

00:17:48.870 --> 00:17:51.120
You guys don't hold back, huh?

00:17:51.580 --> 00:17:54.000
Atsushi-senpai, aren't you going to join in?

00:17:54.320 --> 00:17:55.380
Oh, I am.

00:17:55.840 --> 00:17:58.340
Epinard Love Hurricane!

00:18:02.770 --> 00:18:04.120
Wow.

00:18:04.120 --> 00:18:05.100
Harsh.

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:08.230
Never get on Kinugawa-senpai's bad side, huh?

00:18:15.420 --> 00:18:18.610
You think those trivial attacks 
will be enough to beat me?!

00:18:18.890 --> 00:18:20.570
Well, you do seem to be crying.

00:18:20.570 --> 00:18:23.620
I haven't actually gotten serious yet!

00:18:23.620 --> 00:18:25.580
The real battle is just getting started.

00:18:25.800 --> 00:18:27.650
He's surprisingly tenacious.

00:18:27.650 --> 00:18:28.680
Stubborn's more like it.

00:18:28.680 --> 00:18:30.930
Orifice Tornado!

00:18:33.920 --> 00:18:37.550
<i>JNA flight 62 will begin boarding shortly.</i>

00:18:37.960 --> 00:18:41.880
<i>Boarding passengers please come to gate 21.</i>

00:18:38.990 --> 00:18:40.230
I guess they're not coming.

00:18:41.950 --> 00:18:43.740
Well, it's the Earth Defense Club.

00:18:43.740 --> 00:18:46.050
I guess we shouldn't have 
trusted them to start with.

00:18:46.470 --> 00:18:47.250
They'll come.

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:49.690
At-chan will keep his promise.

00:18:50.680 --> 00:18:53.450
Maybe he got put on day shift,
 or an errand came up?

00:18:53.450 --> 00:18:54.620
Or something...

00:18:56.450 --> 00:18:59.200
<i>JNA will begin boarding shortly.</i>

00:18:59.620 --> 00:19:03.760
<i>Boarding passengers please come to gate 21.</i>

00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:06.640
Let's go.

00:19:06.910 --> 00:19:08.780
We can't be late to board.

00:19:12.080 --> 00:19:13.110
No...

00:19:13.670 --> 00:19:17.460
I must be there to see them off!

00:19:23.360 --> 00:19:25.260
If I defeat you...

00:19:25.430 --> 00:19:28.160
no one will be able to 
move time forward for me!

00:19:28.160 --> 00:19:30.980
I will be eternal!

00:19:31.280 --> 00:19:32.940
Who wants eternity like that?!

00:19:33.160 --> 00:19:33.900
What?!

00:19:34.120 --> 00:19:37.690
Fearing change is like moving backwards!

00:19:38.020 --> 00:19:39.530
Moving forward is

00:19:39.530 --> 00:19:42.700
what lets a person get stronger 
and achieve their dreams!

00:19:43.360 --> 00:19:47.240
So now that we're stronger, 
you can't beat us!

00:19:47.240 --> 00:19:50.370
Wh-Wh-Wh-What?!

00:19:50.590 --> 00:19:51.630
Now!

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:56.000
Sparkle, Lumiere of Love!

00:19:58.520 --> 00:20:00.760
Flash, Purifying Aqua!

00:20:01.730 --> 00:20:04.220
Pierce, Gallant Hurricane!

00:20:05.220 --> 00:20:07.430
Roar, Raging Gaia!

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:10.640
Thrill, Blazing Ignit!

00:20:22.930 --> 00:20:26.990
True Love Attack!

00:20:36.250 --> 00:20:40.300
True Love Fountain!

00:20:52.960 --> 00:20:54.630
Love is over!

00:20:54.630 --> 00:20:56.440
We told you, it's not!

00:20:57.600 --> 00:20:59.310
I know this guy.

00:20:58.940 --> 00:21:01.780
<b>Tokiwa Tomaru</b>

00:20:59.310 --> 00:21:01.780
It's Tokiwa Tomaru from the next class over.

00:21:01.960 --> 00:21:03.860
He was born on April 2nd,

00:21:03.860 --> 00:21:07.470
and really hates being the first 
one in the class to get a year older.

00:21:07.470 --> 00:21:10.240
Even so, you can't stop time.

00:21:10.690 --> 00:21:11.950
Besides...

00:21:10.870 --> 00:21:11.950
<b>Bath Coupon
Kurotama Bath</b>

00:21:11.950 --> 00:21:14.410
Time doesn't betray dreams.

00:21:14.410 --> 00:21:15.940
Actually, I think we're

00:21:15.940 --> 00:21:18.920
on the verge of betraying a dream right now...

00:21:19.070 --> 00:21:20.380
The president's.

00:21:20.980 --> 00:21:22.710
Their flight's about to take off!

00:21:39.460 --> 00:21:40.600
At-chan!

00:21:48.200 --> 00:21:49.070
He noticed!

00:21:49.070 --> 00:21:50.700
He's waving!

00:21:50.700 --> 00:21:53.660
Don't shake me!

00:21:54.210 --> 00:21:56.320
He won't be gone forever.

00:21:56.580 --> 00:21:58.340
He'll be back before you know it.

00:22:01.200 --> 00:22:01.920
Yeah.

00:22:03.080 --> 00:22:03.820
Oh, yeah.

00:22:03.820 --> 00:22:06.100
By the way, where's Mr. Tawarayama?

00:22:06.420 --> 00:22:07.050
Erk!

00:22:07.300 --> 00:22:09.510
A-Actually...

00:22:19.260 --> 00:22:20.110
Hey,

00:22:20.110 --> 00:22:22.780
do you know where the staff office is?

00:22:22.780 --> 00:22:26.010
We're joining Binan High School

00:22:26.410 --> 00:22:29.100
as exchange students.

00:24:00.830 --> 00:24:05.750
<b>Next Time</b>

00:24:00.830 --> 00:24:05.750
Love is a Mayfly

00:24:01.940 --> 00:24:03.910
Next time: "Love is a Mayfly!"

00:24:03.910 --> 00:24:05.440
Love Making!
